        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Is the NordicTrack C950i discontinued?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes. NordicTrack no longer lists it, and Garage Gym Reviews says it is no longer in production. It is only available used.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does iFIT still work on the NordicTrack C950i?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Assume not. iFIT ended support for older-generation machines on 30 April 2023, including those using an external iFIT Wifi Module. Affected machines still work in manual mode and with their preloaded workouts. iFIT can confirm a specific machine at upgrade@ifit.com or 844-867-4562.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the weight limit of the NordicTrack C950i?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              One independent review gives 350 lb, but we found no second source, and NordicTrack folding machines of that era were often rated lower. Read the maximum user weight on the warning decal on the machine and use the lower figure.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the model number of the NordicTrack C950i?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Manual archives list 831.25044.0, and parts catalogues also list 831.25044.2 and 831.25044.5 versions. Check the decal on the frame, since parts can differ between versions.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you still get parts for a NordicTrack C950i?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Common wear parts are listed by third-party sellers: on 5 November 2026 search results showed walking belts around $120 to $130, a drive belt around $38 and a lower motor control board around $200. Match part numbers to your exact model before ordering.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What replaced the NordicTrack C950i?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              NordicTrack has not named a direct successor. The closest current models are the T Series 10, a folding 20 by 60-inch iFIT treadmill, and the sturdier Commercial 1250, which adds decline and a 400 lb rating. Neither reaches the 15% incline one review gives for the C950i.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

